  "id": "attentional-narrowing",
  "term": "attentional narrowing",
  "definition": "Attentional narrowing is a reduced scope of attention in which a person focuses more tightly on emotional information rather than taking in a broader range of cues. In the source packet, it is described as being linked to negative emotion, and more generally as decreased visual attentional breadth.",
